.TITLE "echo"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays a line of text or the value of a variable in the terminal. It is commonly used in __shell scripts__ to provide feedback or create simple files.

.DIV "TLDR"
**echo "message"**
Displays a specific string of text in the terminal window.
> __"message"__ the text to display

**echo $variable**
Displays the current value of an environment or shell variable.
> __$variable__ the name of the variable

**echo -e "line1\nline2"**
Enables the interpretation of backslash escapes like newlines (\n) or tabs (\t).
> __-e__ enable escapes flag | __"line1\nline2"__ text with escapes

**echo -n "message"**
Displays text without appending a newline character at the end.
> __-n__ no newline flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __echo__ with redirection (e.g., __echo "text" > file__) is a quick way to write content to a file. It is a fundamental tool for debugging scripts and verifying that variables are correctly set.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**cli:printf** **cli:cat** **cli:read**

